    "note": "Sourced from the Sri Chaitanya Junior Fastrack zoology section (book p.45, SAQ 52). Zoology holds only ONE source book — the TSBIE Basic Learning Material in hand covers physics only, and no zoology board paper is in the corpus — so the two-book union check and the back-test are both structurally impossible for this card; 'not checked' does NOT mean 'checked and clean'. The mark split is a claim until a Telangana IPE teacher confirms it. APPEARANCES: the book prints [TS May-17,19] and [AP, TS M-15,20]. TEXT BEYOND THE BOOK: the book prints the labelled figure alone with no written answer; the naming lines are authored from the labels the book itself prints. TWO COUNTS ARE NOT PRINTED IN THIS BOOK and are taken from NCERT: about 2000 ommatidia per compound eye, and seven or eight retinular cells per ommatidium — sources differ on the retinular count, so a teacher must settle it. FIGURE SCOPE: the book prints a longitudinal section plus two transverse sections; this card draws the longitudinal section only — lens, corneagen cells, crystalline cone with cone cells, iris pigment sheath, retinular cells with the rhabdom, retinular pigment sheath, basement membrane and nerve fibres."
