        "id": "s1_what",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "What an ommatidium is",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Identity",
        "lines": [
          "An ommatidium is one unit of the compound eye",
          "of the cockroach.",
          "Each compound eye is made of about 2000 such",
          "units.",
          "Each ommatidium is a long cone. It has a",
          "light gathering part above, a light sensitive",
          "part below, and pigment sheaths around them."
        ],
        "why": "Splitting the unit into an upper light gathering part and a lower light sensitive part gives the drawing its two halves, so every named cell can then be placed in one half or the other.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Calling the ommatidium the whole compound eye. It is one unit of it.",
          "Leaving out the pigment sheaths, which are what keep one unit's light separate from the next."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "One eye, about 2000 cones. Each cone: lens on top, rod below, pigment all around.",
        "margin_note": "What it is, how many per eye, and the three regions. Three short lines."
      },
