        "why": "The figure is a stack, and the order down the stack is the path the light takes, so a drawing with the cone below the rhabdom is wrong even when every label is spelled correctly.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing the crystalline cone below the retinular cells. Light meets the lens, then the cone, then the rhabdom.",
          "Drawing the rhabdom outside the retinular cells. It is formed by their inner edges, so it lies in the middle.",
          "Leaving out the basement membrane at the base, through which the nerve fibres leave."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Draw one long narrow cone, then cut it across into three bands: lens on top, crystalline cone next, retinular cells with the rhabdom below.",
        "margin_note": "Both marks are in the labels — lens, corneagen cell, crystalline cone, cone cell, iris pigment sheath, retinular cell, rhabdom, basement membrane, nerve fibres."
